WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.170 --> 00:00:02.820
- Now we all know the only person

00:00:02.820 --> 00:00:04.680
who is just as important as

00:00:04.680 --> 00:00:08.970
the Emmy nominees is
the emcee of the show.

00:00:08.970 --> 00:00:12.720
So let's look back at some of
our favorite Emmy award show

00:00:12.720 --> 00:00:15.240
hosts and their most memorable moments.

00:00:15.240 --> 00:00:16.720
Take a look.

00:00:16.720 --> 00:00:19.530
The Emmy awards have tried
hosts from all across the

00:00:19.530 --> 00:00:21.020
entertainment aisles;

00:00:21.020 --> 00:00:23.700
actors, singers, comedians,

00:00:23.700 --> 00:00:25.730
even a screenwriter was the very first

00:00:25.730 --> 00:00:29.180
host of the Emmy awards in 1949

00:00:29.180 --> 00:00:32.720
and soon followed by some
early television stars,

00:00:32.720 --> 00:00:35.607
including Lucille Ball and Desi Arnaz

00:00:35.607 --> 00:00:40.150
Ed Sullivan, Fred Astaire
and Frank Sinatra.

00:00:40.150 --> 00:00:44.210
In 1975, CBS went with no main hosts,

00:00:44.210 --> 00:00:48.210
but rather 10 mistresses of ceremony.

00:00:48.210 --> 00:00:50.510
Johnny Carson holds the record

00:00:50.510 --> 00:00:53.440
for most Emmys hosted at four.

00:00:53.440 --> 00:00:56.707
While Ellen DeGeneres,
Joey Bishop, John Forsythe,

00:00:56.707 --> 00:01:00.290
Danny Thomas and Jimmy Kimmel
each have hosted three times

00:01:01.280 --> 00:01:03.740
in recent years, late night hosts

00:01:03.740 --> 00:01:07.470
and SNL alums like Andy
Samberg, Stephen Colbert

00:01:07.470 --> 00:01:10.970
and Jimmy Fallon have
traded off hosting duties.

00:01:10.970 --> 00:01:15.290
Fallon opened the Emmy ceremony
with a brilliant epic song

00:01:15.290 --> 00:01:17.950
and dance number in 2010,

00:01:17.950 --> 00:01:19.406
featuring Tina Fey,

00:01:19.406 --> 00:01:20.850
John Hamm

00:01:20.850 --> 00:01:21.870
the cast of Glee,

00:01:21.870 --> 00:01:25.310
and Betty White has been
called the greatest opening

00:01:25.310 --> 00:01:27.350
to the Emmys ever.

00:01:27.350 --> 00:01:31.470
And this year there's a new,
funny man up for the gig.

00:01:31.470 --> 00:01:33.350
Cedric, the entertainer

00:01:33.350 --> 00:01:35.789
has been making us
laugh for over 30 years.

00:01:35.789 --> 00:01:39.690
You've seen him in Barbershop,
Johnson Family Vacation,

00:01:39.690 --> 00:01:41.180
the Steve Harvey show,

00:01:41.180 --> 00:01:46.180
and most currently on the hit
show 'The Neighborhood' on CBS

00:01:46.470 --> 00:01:49.850
And he already has hosting
experience under his belt,

00:01:49.850 --> 00:01:54.100
including a season of 'Who
Wants To Be A Millionaire?'

00:01:54.100 --> 00:01:57.090
We bet this king of comedy is ready to

00:01:57.090 --> 00:01:59.273
hold court at the Emmys.

00:02:01.100 --> 00:02:05.748
Please welcome this year's
73rd annual Emmy awards host.

00:02:05.748 --> 00:02:06.590
(applause)

00:02:06.590 --> 00:02:08.483
Cedric, the Entertainer!

00:02:08.483 --> 00:02:11.824
(crowd cheering)

00:02:11.824 --> 00:02:14.407
(lively music)

00:02:17.066 --> 00:02:18.066
- What's up?

00:02:19.190 --> 00:02:20.773
That's you, you're-

00:02:22.332 --> 00:02:23.165
this is beautiful

00:02:23.165 --> 00:02:23.998
- Well,

00:02:25.098 --> 00:02:25.931
you're-

00:02:25.931 --> 00:02:27.290
- You have great jewelry too.

00:02:27.290 --> 00:02:29.570
Like you're really doing it, Drew.

00:02:29.570 --> 00:02:31.060
You got like great jewelry on

00:02:31.060 --> 00:02:34.130
and see guys, we don't really get to dress

00:02:34.130 --> 00:02:36.700
like really nice jewels.

00:02:36.700 --> 00:02:37.990
- I'm skipping right to
what are you gonna do?

00:02:37.990 --> 00:02:39.710
What are you gonna wear? What'd you think?

00:02:39.710 --> 00:02:40.860
- I mean, you know, it is,

00:02:40.860 --> 00:02:42.670
it's one of those things where
you think you can get away

00:02:42.670 --> 00:02:45.260
with just the black tux and the classic,

00:02:45.260 --> 00:02:46.600
you know, Gable look

00:02:46.600 --> 00:02:49.220
you know, with the pose
and the smoldering eyes.

00:02:49.220 --> 00:02:50.883
I've been working on
that. My eyes smoldered.

00:02:50.883 --> 00:02:51.716
(audience laughs)

00:02:51.716 --> 00:02:53.130
That's all you think
you want to do. Right?

00:02:53.130 --> 00:02:56.360
But now fashion is going a lot forward.

00:02:56.360 --> 00:02:59.730
So, you know, I'm actually
going to change a few times.

00:02:59.730 --> 00:03:01.090
I'm gonna come out with some.

00:03:01.090 --> 00:03:01.923
- Oh, I love that.

00:03:01.923 --> 00:03:02.770
(audience cheers)

00:03:02.770 --> 00:03:04.180
I love that

00:03:04.180 --> 00:03:05.013
Cedric

00:03:05.013 --> 00:03:06.417
Give them what they want.

00:03:06.417 --> 00:03:08.630
- Exactly. Give it to them.

00:03:08.630 --> 00:03:10.567
I'm giving them Magnum.

00:03:10.567 --> 00:03:12.650
(Cheers)

00:03:13.950 --> 00:03:14.790
it works.

00:03:14.790 --> 00:03:18.640
- I love that you get the call to host

00:03:18.640 --> 00:03:20.620
what happens, what takes place?

00:03:20.620 --> 00:03:21.820
What's the circumstances?

00:03:21.820 --> 00:03:22.653
And what goes through your mind?

00:03:22.653 --> 00:03:25.770
- I was like, you know, I was
out pitching another show.

00:03:25.770 --> 00:03:27.610
So, and they like getting you, like,

00:03:27.610 --> 00:03:29.450
you got a call from this
very important person.

00:03:29.450 --> 00:03:33.290
And I was like (chortles) this is the one.

00:03:33.290 --> 00:03:36.420
He was like, Hey yeah, the
thing you tried to sell us.

00:03:36.420 --> 00:03:40.720
That's a no, but would you
want to host the Emmys?

00:03:40.720 --> 00:03:41.803
So, I was like

00:03:41.803 --> 00:03:43.486
hell yeah

00:03:43.486 --> 00:03:46.505
(cheering)

00:03:46.505 --> 00:03:47.753
so I was excited

00:03:47.753 --> 00:03:49.900
that was good. It was one of these.

00:03:49.900 --> 00:03:52.000
It was a bad call. Then it
turned into a good call.

00:03:52.000 --> 00:03:52.930
All in one call.

00:03:52.930 --> 00:03:55.420
- I think the Emmys is
one of my favorite shows

00:03:55.420 --> 00:03:58.760
because I think it's really
representative of the collective

00:03:58.760 --> 00:04:00.523
of the way we're really watching.

00:04:01.515 --> 00:04:03.760
- Yes, I call this the television,

00:04:03.760 --> 00:04:05.080
this is the prom for us.

00:04:05.080 --> 00:04:08.250
This is our night for people
who work in television

00:04:08.250 --> 00:04:09.890
and do this as for a living.

00:04:09.890 --> 00:04:11.719
- Cedric, I know you're
going to be the greatest

00:04:11.719 --> 00:04:15.713
because I've never heard
someone say, this is our prom.

00:04:17.110 --> 00:04:19.270
- It's a coolness that
happens in Hollywood on,

00:04:19.270 --> 00:04:22.100
on those nights when
everybody's kind of dressed up

00:04:22.100 --> 00:04:25.097
and you know, it's this coolness
where we all kind of like

00:04:25.097 --> 00:04:25.930
(tongue clicks)

00:04:25.930 --> 00:04:27.820
- Yeah, listen up, enjoy the moment.

00:04:27.820 --> 00:04:29.330
- Yeah, no, let's turn it.

00:04:29.330 --> 00:04:30.163
Let's do the other thing.

00:04:30.163 --> 00:04:33.293
Let's, I want to be
shirts off jacket-less.

00:04:34.290 --> 00:04:36.240
Yeah, we got to turn up, old school.

00:04:36.240 --> 00:04:38.300
- So your good friend,

00:04:38.300 --> 00:04:41.520
Anthony Anderson is
nominated for lead actor

00:04:41.520 --> 00:04:45.031
in a comedy series. Are
you so happy for him?

00:04:45.031 --> 00:04:47.040
- And you know, and this is probably,

00:04:47.040 --> 00:04:50.240
I think Anthony's eighth nomination

00:04:50.240 --> 00:04:51.960
and so he's never won one.

00:04:51.960 --> 00:04:54.980
So with me being the host, I'm like, bro,

00:04:54.980 --> 00:04:57.680
you leaving out of there
with something, I don't know.

00:05:01.670 --> 00:05:04.580
He's got to get somebody's
Emmy for, you know

00:05:04.580 --> 00:05:06.323
lighting or something and be like,

00:05:07.178 --> 00:05:09.053
"Hey, here you go, dawg. Take that."

00:05:09.053 --> 00:05:09.886
(crowd laughs)

00:05:09.886 --> 00:05:13.140
- No, you're already on a
juggernaut show for CBS,

00:05:13.140 --> 00:05:14.483
'The Neighborhood'

00:05:17.370 --> 00:05:19.550
going into season four.

00:05:19.550 --> 00:05:20.550
I mean.

00:05:20.550 --> 00:05:22.020
How does that feel?

00:05:22.020 --> 00:05:23.387
- I mean, it's very exciting,

00:05:23.387 --> 00:05:24.900
One, I don't take it for granted.

00:05:24.900 --> 00:05:27.460
I've been doing this a
long time and blessed

00:05:27.460 --> 00:05:29.610
to be in television a long time.

00:05:29.610 --> 00:05:31.780
And so we just really blessed
to have the opportunity to

00:05:31.780 --> 00:05:34.700
come back and just to be
able to make people laugh,

00:05:34.700 --> 00:05:37.240
to come into their homes
on Monday nights on CBS,

00:05:37.240 --> 00:05:38.890
Monday nights, eight o'clock guys

00:05:41.770 --> 00:05:42.770
Shameless plug.

00:05:42.770 --> 00:05:44.420
- Thank you, Cedric, the entertainer.

00:05:44.420 --> 00:05:47.630
Be sure to catch the
fourth season of the show

00:05:47.630 --> 00:05:50.590
The Neighborhood on September 20th on CBS

00:05:50.590 --> 00:05:53.836
also streaming on paramount plus

00:05:53.836 --> 00:05:55.750
and tune in to see him

00:05:55.750 --> 00:05:58.410
host the 73rd

00:05:58.410 --> 00:05:59.243
Emmy Awards

00:05:59.243 --> 00:06:02.003
September 19th, on CBS.

